{
  "tema": 6998,
  "slug": "impersonal-ellos",
  "titulo": "Impersonal sentences with the ellos form",
  "subtitulo": "Dicen que va a llover. Tocan la puerta. Me robaron.",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "The third person plural without a subject can mean someone / people / they in general, when we don't know or don't care who did it: Dicen que..., Tocan la puerta, Me robaron la cartera.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Spanish can make a sentence **impersonal** with the **ellos** form of the verb and **no subject**. It means _someone, people, they_, without knowing or caring who."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It works in any tense: **dicen, dijeron, han dicho**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "English has no exact match, so you translate it with _someone, people say, there's..._ or the passive."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Context decides: if the subject was mentioned before, it's just a dropped pronoun, not an impersonal sentence."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: if you can't point at who did it, it's impersonal."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Dicen== que mañana va a llover.",
              "en": "They say it's going to rain tomorrow."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Están llamando== por teléfono.",
              "en": "The phone is ringing. (someone is calling)"
            },
            {
              "es": "¡==Me robaron==!",
              "en": "I've been robbed!"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Tocan== la puerta.",
              "en": "Someone's at the door."
            },
            {
              "es": "En esa fonda ==dan== una comida corrida buenísima.",
              "en": "That diner serves a great set lunch."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Me pusieron== una multa.",
              "en": "I got a ticket."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "contexto",
      "titulo": "Impersonal or not?",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "sujeto conocido",
                  "t": "Carmen y Rosa tocan la puerta."
                },
                {
                  "v": "impersonal",
                  "t": "Tocan la puerta."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "With no expected visitor, **tocan** = _someone is knocking_."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "sujeto omitido",
                  "t": "¡Detengan a esos dos! ¡Me robaron!"
                },
                {
                  "v": "impersonal",
                  "t": "¡Me robaron la cartera en el metro!"
                }
              ],
              "nota": "First: those two did it. Second: who knows."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "otros",
